            <ArticleTitle>Carisoprodol in the treatment of myofascial pain-dysfunction syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>655-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effects of carisoprodol and a placebo were compared in a sample of 60 patients with the clinical diagnosis of myofascial pain-dysfunction syndrome using double-blind design. Carisoprodol failed to show a significantly greater effect than the placebo. The side effects were about the same with both agents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
